 of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span> Clauses as the Subject or Object", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You usually use <span class=\"italic\">that-</span>clauses to talk about facts or beliefs. <br/> <span class=\"italic\">That-</span>clauses can be placed in different parts of the sentence, depending on what you want to communicate.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That-</span>clauses can be the <span class=\"underline\">subject </span>of the sentence. You normally use this structure in formal writing or speaking.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">That we don't care </span>is simply not true.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is more common to use the structure <span class=\"italic\">It ... that ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It </span>is simply not true <span class=\"strong\">that we don't care</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use a that-clause as the <span class=\"underline\">object </span> (after reporting verbs), you often omit <span class=\"italic\">that</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">She promised <span class=\"strong\">(that) she would come.</span></span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I just got the text (that) you sent yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I got it at the exact same time (that) you sent it yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think (that) there's something wrong with my phone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I showed him the text (that) I had received. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking for and Offering Help with Technical Problems", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are many ways to ask for and offer help in English. Some are more formal than others.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Offering  Help\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Asking for Help\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could you do me a favor? <br/> Could I ask you a favor? <br/>  Can I ask you to ... ?<br/> I need some help (if you have time). <br/> (If you're not busy) I could use your help.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Do you need some help with your laptop?</li> <li>What can I do?</li> <li>Tell me how I can help.</li> </ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Offering Help\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">May I help you? <br/> Can I help you? <br/> Are you looking for something? <br/> Would you like some help? <br/> Do you need some help? <br/> What can I do for you today?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li> I wonder if you could do me a favor. </li> <li>Can I ask you to send me an e-mail? </li> </ul></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "odd", "type": "name"}, {"content": "strange or unexpected", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have received some odd e-mails from you. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about strange events and coincidences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to back up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to copy information to a separate location in case the original copy is lost or damaged", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you backed up your phone?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "glitch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a problem or fault", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There's some sort of glitch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bizarre", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unconventional; eccentric", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Isn't that bizarre?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mortifying", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very embarrassing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Oh, this is mortifying.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "precisely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "exactly accurate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I got it at precisely the same time that you sent it yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On a piece of paper, write down five possible things that could go wrong with different types of technology.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Get together with a partner and show him or her your list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Together, talk about some ways to solve each of your technological problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do the same with your partner's list of technological problems.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make a list of technological problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss solutions to technological problems with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make suggestions and give advice. ", "type": "text"}]}]}